(D2 — Discrepancy 2 repro: LANGUAGE.md:2381-2383 says a `For each` over a
 list of maps "types the loop variable as a map". It does not: the loop
 variable carries the map TAG (so `is a map` fires on it — LST-55) but has
 no static type, and map access is a static check, so `entry's "tag"`
 inside the loop is a compile error. Extracting the element into a declared
 `map` variable first works (LST-57).
